# NGA SDK License

Version 1.1 · Effective 11 November 2026

This license is between NGA Network, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company ("**NGA**", "**we**"), and the person or company that downloads, installs or uses the NGA SDK ("**you**"). A studio accepts this license, together with NGA's Studio Terms and Data Processing Agreement, when it signs up in NGA's portal, and must do so before any integration of the NGA SDK sends real player data to NGA, including for testing. Before signing up, you may download the NGA SDK and evaluate it offline, without activating NGA's services. Anyone else who downloads, installs or uses the NGA SDK agrees to this license by doing so. If you accept this license on behalf of a company, you confirm you can bind that company.

## What this license covers

The "**NGA SDK**" means NGA's software development kit in every form NGA makes it available, together with its documentation, and any updates NGA provides. Its forms include:

- the Android libraries network.nga:nga-sdk and network.nga:nga-sdk-render;
- the iOS frameworks NGASDK and NGASDKRender;
- the Unity packages network.nga.sdk and network.nga.sdk-render.

"**Your App**" means a mobile application or game that you own or have the right to publish.

## What you may do

NGA grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free, worldwide, revocable license, for as long as this license lasts:

- to integrate the NGA SDK, unmodified, into Your Apps and test it, yourself or through your employees and contractors acting on your behalf, who must follow this license and for whom you are responsible;
- to distribute the NGA SDK to end users only as part of the compiled builds of Your Apps, through app stores or your own channels, and to let app stores distribute those builds;
- to use the documentation and sample code to do so. You may modify sample code for that purpose.

## NGA's services

The NGA SDK connects Your Apps to NGA's services, such as cross-promotion, advertising and measurement. Your use of those services is governed by NGA's Studio Terms and Data Processing Agreement, which a studio accepts when it signs up in NGA's portal. If they conflict with this license on the use of the services, the Studio Terms govern.

## What you may not do

Except as this license expressly allows, or as applicable law permits notwithstanding this restriction, you may not, and may not let anyone else:

- modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the NGA SDK. Compiling, linking, minifying, obfuscating, stripping and signing the NGA SDK as part of Your Apps, and configuring it as its documentation describes, are not modification;
- decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the NGA SDK, or try to derive its source code;
- distribute, sell, lease or sublicense the NGA SDK on its own, or as part of any SDK, library, framework or developer tool;
- remove or alter any notice of ownership or license in the NGA SDK;
- circumvent or interfere with the NGA SDK's security, integrity or fraud-prevention features, or alter, fabricate or replay the data it sends to NGA;
- use the NGA SDK to build or train a competing product or service;
- use the NGA SDK in an app that breaks applicable law or the policies of the app store it is distributed through.

## Third-party components

The NGA SDK may include components from third parties, including open-source software. Those components are licensed under their own terms, which are listed in the NGA SDK's notices file. Nothing in this license limits your rights under those terms.

## Data and privacy

The NGA SDK collects and sends data as its documentation describes. You are responsible for the disclosures and consents the law and the app stores require of Your Apps, as set out in the Studio Terms and the Data Processing Agreement.

## Ownership and feedback

NGA and its licensors own the NGA SDK and all rights in it. This license grants no rights other than those it expressly states. If you send NGA feedback or suggestions about the NGA SDK, NGA may use them without obligation to you.

## Updates and retired versions

NGA may release updates to the NGA SDK. A supported version keeps working with NGA's services and receives critical and security fixes, but not new features. From the first stable version, 1.0, NGA supports each minor version for at least 24 months after its release, and gives at least 6 months' notice before retiring one. A preview or release-candidate version (any 0.x version, and any version marked -rc.N) is supported until NGA makes its next version generally available, whether a preview, a release candidate or a stable version, and for 3 months after that. Support for any version applies only while the NGA services it works with remain available. NGA may stop serving a version immediately, without notice, when it is needed to protect players, studios or NGA's services, for example after a security or data problem. Retiring a version ends support for that version only. It does not end this license or a studio's account, which end only as "Term and termination" and the Studio Terms describe.

## Term and termination

This license lasts until it is terminated:

- **By you:** at any time, by stopping all use and distribution of the NGA SDK.
- **By NGA:** on 30 days' notice to you, for any reason. If you materially breach this license and the breach can be remedied, NGA may terminate it if you have not remedied the breach within 15 days after NGA's notice. NGA may terminate it immediately for a material breach that cannot be remedied, and may suspend or terminate it immediately for security reasons, where the law requires it, to stop fraud or abuse, or for sanctions reasons. For a studio, this license also ends when its Studio Terms end.

When this license ends:

- NGA stops serving ads and cross-promotion to Your Apps, and you must stop new integrations of the NGA SDK;
- you must remove it from each of Your Apps in the ordinary course of your updates to that App. There is no fixed deadline, because players on older builds may never update;
- copies already installed on end users' devices may remain until those devices update. Data those copies send to NGA continues to be received and processed under the Data Processing Agreement and the Studio Terms' data terms, which continue for as long as such builds send data, and you must keep your privacy notice covering it. You may instruct NGA in writing at any time to stop accepting data from Your Apps. NGA does so within 5 business days, and then deletes that data as the Data Processing Agreement describes.

"What you may not do", "Data and privacy", "Ownership and feedback", "No warranty", "Limitation of liability", "Export and sanctions", "Governing law" and "Changes to this license" survive termination.

